================================================================================
## English/Korean UI internationalisation ported onto 0.9.0 + Korean for the 0.9.0 UI
================================================================================

Context:
The client-side i18n layer (global/js/i18n.js + the flat Korean dictionary
global/js/i18n-ko.js, `ob_lang` cookie, `ONTOBRICKS_UI_LANG` deploy default,
`data-i18n-skip` for user content) was re-applied on top of 0.9.0. 0.9.0
added a large amount of new UI copy (Studio, 3-step ontology Generate, SPARQL
playground, Find Path, SHACL data-quality facets, entity panel regroup with
Functions / Databricks Jobs / Inference rules, GitHub mirror, version delete
safeguards, audit before/after, Build vs Query SQL Warehouse and Lakehouse//RT,
CloudFetch toggle, AI Gateway LLM picker, data assets import limit, Knowledge
Store, "Information" renamed to "General", ...) that had no Korean entries, so
the coverage ratchet failed and Korean users saw those screens in English.
Only application chrome is translated; entity / attribute / domain / rule /
job names, descriptions, query results and audit values stay verbatim.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/global/js/i18n-ko.js
   678 new Korean entries: every
   template and script string the coverage test reported, the five new menu
   labels, and the JS-built runtime messages of the new modules (toasts,
   confirm dialogs, `{n}` count templates, status chips). Renamed terms
   follow the old choices: Data Assets → 데이터 자산, Knowledge Store →
   지식 스토어, General → 일반, Studio → 스튜디오; Job stays "Job".
   46 entries whose English 0.9.0 no longer shows (mostly "Data Source(s)",
   renamed to "Data Asset(s)") were removed; their new wording has entries.
   "Cohort Discovery" now reads 세그먼트 탐색, matching "Cohort discovery".
2. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js,
   ontology-wizard-review.js, ontology-entity-import.js,
   src/front/static/query/js/query-find-path.js, query-shacl-facets.js,
   query-business-rules.js, query-dashboard.js, query-execute.js,
   src/front/static/global/js/llm-endpoint-picker.js, navbar.js,
   src/front/static/domain/js/domain-audit.js, domain-versions.js
   `data-i18n-skip` on script-rendered user content: entity panel item
   titles / meta / descriptions and axiom chips, Generate review labels and
   alternate labels, entity-import names, Find Path picks, SHACL shape labels
   and messages, business-rule and Job popup titles / descriptions / result
   rows, LLM endpoint names, audit asset / old / new values, actors and
   comments, version descriptions and authors. SPARQL results and the navbar
   / workspace-map domain name toggle the marker so their placeholders stay
   translatable.
3. src/front/templates/partials/domain/_domain_versions.html
   The version card list is no longer skipped wholesale, so status badges and
   action buttons translate (user fields are skipped per element).
4. src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_shacl_facets_modal.html,
   _query_sigmagraph.html
   Skip markers on the SHACL facet entity / subtitle and the Find Path
   suggestion lists.
5. src/front/templates/partials/ontology/_ontology_business_rules.html,
   partials/settings/_settings_github.html
   `translate="no"` on example identifiers (riskTier = high, HighRiskCustomer,
   VipCustomer, hasOrder, amount) and example placeholders (my-org,
   ontobricks-ontologies, main, ontobricks@example.com).
6. tests/units/front/test_i18n.py
   GitHub added to the keep-in-English menu names; user-content roots updated
   for 0.9.0 (removed versionsTableBody / ucBrowserFilesList, added SHACL
   facet and Find Path roots); new checks for the script-rendered skip
   markers, the version card list and the name/placeholder toggles.
7. tests/units/front/i18n_untranslated_baseline.json
   Stale entries removed (6); added only product names / acronyms ((Postgres),
   AI Gateway, CSV, LLM, Spark SQL), the OWL term Class, two sentence
   connectors (The, with), exported build-log text titles, audit field keys
   (label, message), the schedule label fragment "graph cache refresh", and
   the first literal of concatenated messages whose full runtime text is in
   the dictionary or embeds user names.

